    "updated_at": "2025-06-13T23:08:15Z",
    "body": "Ah thanks, yeah, `react to a promise` works fine for ensuring you actually get a T out (anything else will either convert to a T via the standard rules, or throw an error, and I don't believe spec text needs to handle errors explicitly; it'll get auto-caught by the IDL machinery and cause a rejected promise).\n\nSo yeah, it's just the fact that `T` can be passed to a `promise<T>` argument that should be spelled out (in a note).",
